<resources>
    <!--
      Google Material 3 (GM3) system color tokens: the static palette Google apps use
      (Messages, Gmail, Drive, Calendar, etc.), not the purple AndroidX M3 baseline.

      CSS custom properties are named gm3-sys-color-* (with a double-hyphen prefix in CSS;
      XML comments cannot contain that prefix, so it is written without the leading hyphens).

      Sources (cross-checked; every hex below appears in at least one):
      1. Complete light + dark gm3-sys-color-* CSS (Google Calendar style dump mirrored at):
         https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pabricrui/web/49df1f1c1cca8853ac985a419cc8d3fe33954fd3/css/material.css
      2. Same light/dark gm3-sys-color-* set:
         https://raw.githubusercontent.com/WalkQuackBack/review-app-vite/7e8184ab78d4ec974cf9ccbf3967069f3d72901c/src/styles/globals.css
      3. Light hex to gm3-sys-color-* map extracted from Google Workspace CSS:
         https://raw.githubusercontent.com/WalkQuackBack/google-suite-color-theme/main/color-index.ts
      4. com_google_material_gm3V10 / gm3V11 asset-catalog roles (light/dark) from a Google app dump:
         https://techdevnotes.com/apps/ios/gemini/6477489729/design-system

      Corrections vs an earlier draft that used on-*-fixed tones for container on roles:
      - Light onPrimaryContainer is #0842A0 (sources 1 and 4), not #041E49 (#041E49 is on-primary-fixed).
        Source 2 lists #041E49 for on-primary-container; we follow 1 and 4 (and source 1's on-primary-fixed-variant).
      - Light onSecondaryContainer is #004A77 (sources 1 and 4), not #001D35 (#001D35 is on-secondary-fixed).
        Source 2 lists #001D35 for on-secondary-container; we follow 1 and 4.
      - Light onErrorContainer is #8C1D18 (sources 1 and 4); source 2 lists #410E0B; we follow 1 and 4.

      Scrim dim alphas (60%/70% black) are app lift/modal overlays on top of GM3 scrim #000000.
    -->

